gsnprov:dd-0115
    a gsnprov:RetiredDecision ;
    gsnprov:retirementReason "domain widened to the four classes the rules actually mark valid in 1.2.3. The single-class domain excluded relationships, arguments and patterns, so rules S20, S21, S22, S29 and S31 all produced data the ontology rejected. gsn:Relationship was widened into the domain rather than made a subclass of gsn:GSNElement, because that class requires exactly one schema:identifier and subclassing would have forced an identifier onto every reified relationship. Superseded by the widened domain recorded in the same release."@en ;
    gsnprov:positionKey "S03.R034" ;
    gsnprov:part gsnprov:part-0 ;
    gsnprov:section gsnprov:sec-part0-glossary ;
    gsnprov:formalism gsnprov:OWL ;
    gsnprov:naturalLanguage "Only a GSN element can be marked as ‘valid’."@en ;
    gsnprov:nlWrittenFor "cb124895" ;
    prov:used gsnprov:src-0033 ;
    prov:generated gsnprov:st-0115 .

