gsnprov:dd-0150
    a gsnprov:RetiredDecision ;
    gsnprov:retirementReason "the inverse-support restriction was widened to gsn:Goal or gsn:Strategy in 1.2.3. Reading it over goals alone meant only a goal reached directly from another goal counted as parented, so every goal whose parent is a strategy, which is the ordinary shape of a decomposed argument, was inferred to be a top goal. Those two classes are exactly the rdfs:domain of gsn:supportedBy, so naming one of them was a formalization slip rather than a claim about the notation. Superseded by the widened axiom recorded in the same release."@en ;
    gsnprov:positionKey "S03.R064" ;
    gsnprov:part gsnprov:part-0 ;
    gsnprov:section gsnprov:sec-part0-glossary ;
    gsnprov:formalism gsnprov:OWL ;
    gsnprov:naturalLanguage "A goal is marked as a top goal exactly when it supports no other goal."@en ;
    gsnprov:nlWrittenFor "0268ec1d" ;
    prov:used gsnprov:src-0041 ;
    gsnprov:hasRationale gsnprov:why-0024 ;
    prov:generated gsnprov:st-0150 .

